IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `df80-nouns`
IMPORT `df80-cross-references`

-- Row il-80. TESTS OF THE CONTROLS: the sound readings kept beside the defects. They pass.
-- Each control shows that the test finds what it looks for where it is there, so that a failing test in df80-tests-red.l4 is a finding and not a test that cannot succeed.
-- The expected values are written from the printed pages and from NOTES.md, not copied from the values in df80-cross-references.l4.

§ `Tests of the controls`

-- I1 control 1: the test for a name printed with the word בטלה finds the name in section 30 of the Commissions of Inquiry Law, where the page prints both.
#ASSERT `the name is printed with the word בטלה in a text in the list` "פקודת ועדות חקירה" (LIST `section 30 of the Commissions of Inquiry Law as printed in SH 548`)

-- I1 control 2: the same test says no for a name that section 30 does not print.
#ASSERT NOT (`the name is printed with the word בטלה in a text in the list` "חוק־יסוד: הכנסת" (LIST `section 30 of the Commissions of Inquiry Law as printed in SH 548`))

-- I1 control 3: the 1967 deletion, replayed on paragraph (6), leaves the name in the words (the test finds the name where it is).
#ASSERT CONTAINS `paragraph (6) after the 1967 deletion, replayed literally` "פקודת ועדות חקירה"

-- I1 control 4: the name in section 30 of the 1968 Law and the name in paragraph (6) are the same string.
#ASSERT `the name in section 30 of the Commissions of Inquiry Law` EQUALS `the name in paragraph (6) of section 13`

-- I1 control 5: paragraph (5)(ב) of section 15 reaches paragraph (6) by the pointer 13(6) and does not contain the name.
#ASSERT CONTAINS (`paragraph (5)(ב) of section 15 as printed in SH 464`'s `its words`) "13(6)"
#ASSERT NOT (CONTAINS (`paragraph (5)(ב) of section 15 as printed in SH 464`'s `its words`) "פקודת ועדות חקירה")

-- I1 control 6: the Basic Law named in paragraph (6) is typed as not checked, and the Ordinance as read from the page.
#ASSERT `the Basic Law named in paragraph (6)`'s `how the row read it` EQUALS `not checked`
#ASSERT `the Ordinance named in paragraph (6)`'s `how the row read it` EQUALS `official page image`

-- I1 control 7: the three parts of paragraph (6), put back with the deleted string at both places, equal the words of the page.
#ASSERT `paragraph (6), the three parts put back with the deleted string at both places` EQUALS `paragraph (6) of section 13 as printed in SH 464`'s `its words`

-- I2 control 1: the table prints lettered old numbers where there are some, so that the failure of Red 1 below is not the table leaving out letters.
#ASSERT `some row prints the letter after its old section number` "א" `the rows of the double column second from the left, from old 55alef to old 56`
#ASSERT `some row prints the letter after its old section number` "ב" `the rows of the double column second from the left, from old 55alef to old 56`
#ASSERT `some row prints the letter after its old section number` "ג" `the rows of the double column second from the left, from old 55alef to old 56`

-- I2 control 2: the old-section cells of the deposited bands do contain 55ב (the rows exist), and section 7's own words contain 55ב after the 1967 insertion and not before it.
#ASSERT `some old-section cell contains the words` "55ב" `all the rows typed from the deposited bands`
#ASSERT CONTAINS `section 7 after the 1967 insertion, replayed literally` "55ב"
#ASSERT NOT (CONTAINS (`section 7 as printed in SH 464`'s `its words`) "55ב")

-- I2 control 3: the test for a row printed between two rows finds one where there is one: the row for old 3 (proviso) lies between the rows for old 3 (opening part) and old 4(1).
#ASSERT `a row whose old-section cell is the cell is printed between two rows` `old 3 opening part` `old 4(1)` "3 תנאי" `the rows of the right-hand double column, from old 2(1) to old 15`

-- I2 control 4: the test for a new-section cell that prints given words finds them for the row of old 55א, whose new-section cell prints 63.
#ASSERT `some row for the old section prints the words in its new-section cell` 55 "א" "63" `the rows of the double column second from the left, from old 55alef to old 56`

-- I2 control 5: the 1967 instruction names 55ב as the words to insert, after the characters 15.
#ASSERT `SH 508 item 4 inserts words in section 7`'s `the words it names` EQUALS "55ב"
#ASSERT `SH 508 item 4 inserts words in section 7`'s `the words it comes after` EQUALS JUST "15"
